notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-05T19:20:27.628Z","harness:claude-code","PROBABILITY CORRECTION (raised in review by CodeRabbit, P2).\n\nThis item's description states the per-run setup failure probability as 6.4e-5. That figure is WRONG and is superseded by this note.\n\n6.4e-5 counts all THREE id pairs (3 x 36^-3). But the assertion only fails when the SELECTED TARGET's prefix is ambiguous, and a pair between the two non-target ids cannot make the target ambiguous. Only the two pairs involving the target count:\n\n  1 - (1 - 36^-3)^2 = 4.29e-5\n\nThe issue's own simulation already agreed with the corrected model and not the original one: 16 failures in 400,000 trials is 4.0e-5, which matches the two-pair figure of 4.29e-5, not the three-pair figure of 6.4e-5. The empirical evidence was in the issue from the start and was read against the wrong model.\n\nConsequences for the implemented fix: none. The bound of 8 attempts was chosen with margin, and at the corrected probability exhaustion is below 1.2e-35 rather than the 1e-33 originally documented, so the fix is if anything safer than claimed. The source comment in test/id-resolution.test.ts now carries the corrected figure.\n\nNot rewriting the earlier history entries: the history ledger is append-only and audited, so a superseded figure is corrected by appending this note rather than by editing the record that stated it."
close_reason: "Both flaky setups replaced with one shared bounded-retry chain builder; workspace leak on the throw path closed; probability corrected to 4.29e-5 in code and tracker. PR #54 merged with all checks green, 195/195 tests, and two bot rounds resolved."
